  "tagline": "Lightweight, fast native XML database and XQuery 3.1/4.0 processor with a GUI.",
  "description": "BaseX is a compact Java XML database and XQuery processor known for fast query evaluation, standards conformance and a useful visual GUI for exploring documents. It supports XQuery 3.1 (with growing XQuery 4.0 support), XQuery Full Text, XQuery Update and RESTXQ for building web services, and it can also store and query JSON, CSV and binary files. It runs embedded, as a client/server database or as an HTTP server, and releases arrive several times a year (12.4 in May 2026) from a small, dedicated team. It is a strong, permissively licensed choice for XML processing and document-centric apps on a single machine.",
